  "expectations": {
    "E01": "Accept exact mapping as metadata only, with parent-published fixture lock. No real output directory or scientific import.",
    "E02": "Source-v3 CLI forwards exact spec/config/context to fixed benign sentinel at scratch output only; no scientific module import; full matching profile manifest.",
    "E03": "Mutate only named component of otherwise admitted clean fixture; parent publishes its expected lock digest when testing inner validation. Refuse named gate before output or sentinel, retain exact bytes/error identity.",
    "E04": "After genuine initial admission, mutate only disposable copy of named file/state; refuse before mkdir/child with exact failed predicate.",
    "E05": "After normal child start, mutate only disposable named fixture file/state; retain its before/after bytes and exact false postflight predicate; valid remains false.",
    "E06": "Omit one declared stdout.txt; parent must either create its owned exact capture before finalization or report missing artifact, never silently drop frozen filename.",
    "E07": "Benign fixture omits one nonlog original profile file. Final validity false; missing list exact; do not fabricate placeholder scientific output.",
    "E08": "Fixture-owned aliases/barrier race stay inside scratch; target hash unchanged; exclusive no-follow creation refuses; full alias metadata and terminal diagnostic preserved. No mutation of real source or user files.",
    "E09": "Barrier observation shows complete flushed/fsynced companions/profile hashing before exclusive final manifest publication; manifest contains no self-hash.",
    "E10": "A scratch-only actor creates reserved manifest path at explicit barrier before publication; no overwrite, deterministic refusal and preserved preexisting bytes. Record actual race outcome; static inspection is not a raced control.",
    "E11": "Only explicitly allowed benign canary is present with exact configured value; inherited disallowed canary absent; no secret environment values read or archived.",
    "E12": "Introduce a single undeclared fixture tree file after start; fail only tree check where all other predicates remain true; compare against clean same-shape baseline.",
    "E13": "Replace disposable source file with byte-identical different inode between phases; identity drift refuses even though SHA remains equal.",
    "E14": "Declared root/non-POSIX/missing resource support case refuses in deterministic metadata check; label actual host mechanism untested if no appropriate host was used; never escalate or invoke root for this control."
  },
